an></span></div></label><div class=\"sk-toggleable__content fitted\"><pre>KNeighborsClassifier(n_neighbors=9)</pre></div> </div></div></div></div>"]},"metadata":{},"execution_count":87}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Comprehensive Metrics: Plot the confusion matrix for both models side-by-side. Instead of just Accuracy, print a DataFrame comparing Recall, Precision, F1-Score, and ROC-AUC Score for both models (focusing on the \"Default=1\" class)."],"metadata":{"id":"JTnZDOpaaHre"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["from sklearn.metrics import confusion_matrix, classification_report, roc_curve, auc, ConfusionMatrixDisplay, recall_score, precision_score, f1_score, roc_auc_score\n","\n","# Logistic Regression\n","y_pred_log = log_reg.predict(X_test)\n","y_proba_log = log_reg.predict_proba(X_test)[:, 1]   # prob de Default=1\n","\n","# KNN\n","y_pred_knn = knn.predict(X_test)\n","y_proba_knn = knn.predict_proba(X_test)[:, 1]       # prob de Default=1"],"metadata":{"id":"cOV30ZbsaJtg"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(10, 4))\n","\n","# LogReg\n","ConfusionMatrixDisplay.from_predictions(y_test,y_pred_log,display_labels=[\"No Default\", \"Default\"],cmap=\"Blues\",ax=axes[0])\n","axes[0].set_title(\"Logistic Regression\")\n","\n","# KNN\n","ConfusionMatrixDisplay.from_predictions(y_test,y_pred_knn,display_labels=[\"No Default\", \"Default\"],cmap=\"Blues\", ax=axes[1])\n","axes[1].set_title(\"KNN (k=9)\")\n","\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()\n"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":388},"id":"Vsi5kfBbcaGH","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1764535567034,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":357,"user":{"displayName":"Melany Moreno","userId":"15591467583801099581"}},"outputId":"f1a8684f-9e70-4cf6-e127-b06c26af8910"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x400 with 4 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["TP = 32 vs 11 in KNN------FN = 59 vs 80 in KNN.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"XdOY-v62dlgz"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["rows = []\n","\n","for model_name, y_pred, y_proba in [\n","    (\"Logistic Regression\", y_pred_log, y_proba_log),\n","    (\"KNN (k=9)\", y_pred_knn, y_proba_knn),\n","]:\n","    rows.append({\n","        \"Model\": model_name,\n","        \"Recall (Default=1)\": recall_score(y_test, y_pred),\n","        \"Precision (Default=1)\": precision_score(y_test, y_pred),\n","        \"F1 (Default=1)\": f1_score(y_test, y_pred),\n","        \"ROC-AUC\": roc_auc_score(y_test, y_proba)\n","    })\n","\n","metrics_df = pd.DataFrame(rows).set_index(\"Model\")\n","print(metrics_df)\n"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"yzSel96Mc025","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1764535567037,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":49,"user":{"displayName":"Melany Moreno","userId":"15591467583801099581"}},"outputId":"2d2d6f39-1771-426f-f9f3-d58f4e886845"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["                     Recall (Default=1)  Precision (Default=1)  \\\n","Model                                                            \n","Logistic Regression            0.351648               0.695652   \n","KNN (k=9)                      0.120879               0.611111   \n","\n","                     F1 (Default=1)   ROC-AUC  \n","Model                                          \n","Logistic Regression        0.467153  0.935566  \n","KNN (k=9)                  0.201835  0.829593  \n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The Trade-off Analysis:\n","Recall: Which model is safer (misses fewer defaults)?\n","Precision: Which model is more efficient (falsely accuses fewer good customers)?\n","F1-Score: Which model provides the best balance?"],"metadata":{"id":"kgWMlCiAaKA_"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["TP (True Positive): predigo positivo y es positivo de verdad.\n","\n","FP (False Positive): predigo positivo y es negativo (falsa alarma).\n","\n","TN (True Negative): predigo negativo y es negativo.\n","\n","FN (False Negative): predigo negativo y es positivo (se me escapó el positivo)."],"metadata":{"id":"IM8Yh8cjTaAX"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["En un problema de clasificación, **accuracy** mide el porcentaje total de aciertos: ((TP + TN)/(TP + TN + FP + FN)), pero puede ser engañoso si la clase positiva es rara ( o sea un grupo normal con pocos defaults); **precision** mide, de todo lo que el modelo predijo como positivo, qué proporción realmente lo es: (TP/(TP + FP)), y es importante cuando es grave etiquetar como positivo a alguien que en realidad es negativo (falsos positivos); **recall** mide, de todos los positivos reales, qué proporción detecta el modelo: (TP/(TP + FN)), y es clave cuando es grave que se escape un positivo real (falsos negativos).\n"],"metadata":{"id":"whMsnNXaTxMU"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["\n","RECALL: LogReg: 0.35 catches 35% of true defaulters.\n","\n","KNN: 0.12 only 12% of defaulters.\n","\n","PRECISION: LogReg: 0.70 so when it predicts default, it’s right 70% of the time.\n","\n","KNN: 0.61,lower\n","\n","F1 SCORE: LogReg: 0.47\n","\n","KNN: 0.20\n","\n","LogReg dominates KNN.\n","\n","ROC-AUC\n","\n","LogReg: 0.94\n","\n","KNN: 0.83\n","LogReg ranks customers by risk much better than KNN.\n","\n","conclusion: Logistic Regression clearly outperforms KNN.\n","It has a higher recall wich means  it identifies many more actual defaulters, and also has a  higher precision, so its default predictions are more reliable. This results in a   better F1-score for the default.\n","In addition, Logreg achieves a higher ROC-AUC indicating that it is much better at ranking customers according to their risk level.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"BM7C_EkSd-eH"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Visualizing Performance: Plot the ROC Curve for both models on the same graph. Which curve is closer to the top-left corner?\n","\n","\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"UMcX96hWaL6Q"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["\n","# ROC points for each model -\n","fpr_log, tpr_log, _ = roc_curve(y_test, y_proba_log)\n","fpr_knn, tpr_knn, _ = roc_curve(y_test, y_proba_knn)\n","\n","auc_log = auc(fpr_log, tpr_log)\n","auc_knn = auc(fpr_knn, tpr_knn)\n","\n","\n","plt.figure(figsize=(6, 5))\n","# LogReg ROC curve\n","plt.plot(fpr_log, tpr_log, label=f\"Logistic Regression (AUC = {auc_log:.3f})\")\n","## KNN ROC curve\n","plt.plot(fpr_knn, tpr_knn, label=f\"KNN (k=9) (AUC = {auc_knn:.3f})\")\n","plt.xlabel(\"False Positive Rate\")\n","plt.ylabel(\"True Positive Rate\")\n","plt.title(\"ROC Curve: Logistic Regression vs KNN\")\n","plt.legend(loc=\"lower right\")\n","plt.grid(True)\n","plt.show()\n","\n"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":487},"id":"RVo-eZg8aPo5","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1764535567441,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":403,"user":{"displayName":"Melany Moreno","userId":"15591467583801099581"}},"outputId":"8151237c-b44e-441d-9fc9-eab2c0a2a457"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 600x500 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["LogReg is closer from the left corner and is always above the knn, meaning that LogReg is better.It will catch more defaulters,without increasing the false positives."],"metadata":{"id":"Ek_VT_PWfm6o"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The Verdict: As a Risk Manager, you must choose one model to deploy.\n","Scenario A: Your bank is conservative and fears losing principal (Needs high Recall). Which model do you pick?\n","\n","Scenario B: Your bank wants to grow and fears rejecting good customers (Needs high Precision). Which model do you pick?\n","\n","Final Decision: Considering Explainability (Part 2) and Performance (Part 3), which model is the most realistic choice for a regulated financial institution?"],"metadata":{"id":"1J3-fhE_aPYS"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Scenario A: need high recall, so it will pick LogReg because this one finds many more of the real defaulters and leaves fewer risky customers undetected.\n","Scenario B: need high precision, so it will pick Log Reg, because is a model that usually when say defaults is because it's right, so only few good customers are incorrectly flagged as risky costumers.This model is more accurate when it labels someone as default.\n","\n","Final decision: Logistic Regression wins on Recall, Precision, F1 and ROC-AUC.It gives better risk detection and is transparent and interpretable."],"metadata":{"id":"9ZX5GiIZgIOL"}}]}